## 3. DESIGN TOKENS & VISUAL HIERARCHY

### 3.1. Canonical Color Tokens (Light & Warm Espresso Dark Theme)
Use ONLY these CSS variables. Never invent new color variables.

```css
:root {
  /* Surfaces (Light) */
  --bg-app: #f4f5f7;
  --bg-card: #ffffff;
  --bg-card-sub: #f8fafc;
  --bg-input: #eef0f4;
  --glass-bg: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);

  /* Typography (Cool Slate Hierarchy) */
  --text-main: #0f172a;
  --text-sub: #475569;
  --text-faint: #94a3b8;

  /* Borders & Elevations */
  --border-line: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
  --border-divider: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
  --shadow-soft: 0 2px 8px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.04);
  --shadow-float: 0 12px 32px -4px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.12);

  /* Semantic Accents (Apple HIG) */
  --c-brand: #ee5d36;
  --c-brand-bg: rgba(238, 93, 54, 0.12);
  --c-blue: #007aff;
  --c-blue-bg: rgba(0, 122, 255, 0.12);
  --c-green: #10b981;
  --c-green-bg: rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.12);
  --c-amber: #f59e0b;
  --c-amber-bg: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.14);
  --c-coral: #ef4444;
  --c-coral-bg: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.12);
  --c-cyan: #06b6d4;
  --c-cyan-bg: rgba(6, 182, 212, 0.12);

  /* Radii (4 Strict Steps) */
  --radius-sm: 8px;
  --radius-md: 12px;
  --radius-lg: 16px;
  --radius-full: 9999px;

  /* Motion Curves */
  --spring-ios: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  --ease-out-expo: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
}

[data-theme="dark"] {
  /* Warm Espresso Surfaces (FnBOps Signature Luxury) */
  --bg-app: #12100e;
  --bg-card: #1c1917;
  --bg-card-sub: #26221f;
  --bg-input: #2e2925;
  --glass-bg: rgba(28, 25, 23, 0.88);

  /* Warm Stone Typography (Zero Muddy Green #b2c2a6) */
  --text-main: #fafaf9;
  --text-sub: #d6d3d1;
  --text-faint: #a8a29e;

  --border-line: rgba(255, 248, 240, 0.08);
  --border-divider: rgba(255, 248, 240, 0.05);
  --shadow-soft: 0 4px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);

  --c-brand: #ff6b47;
  --c-brand-bg: rgba(255, 107, 71, 0.18);
  --c-blue: #0a84ff;
  --c-blue-bg: rgba(10, 132, 255, 0.18);
  --c-green: #30d158;
  --c-green-bg: rgba(48, 209, 88, 0.18);
  --c-amber: #ff9f0a;
  --c-amber-bg: rgba(255, 159, 10, 0.18);
  --c-coral: #ff453a;
  --c-coral-bg: rgba(255, 69, 58, 0.18);
  --c-cyan: #64d2ff;
  --c-cyan-bg: rgba(100, 210, 255, 0.18);
}
```

### 3.2. Visual Hierarchy Laws ("Quiet by Default, Loud on Exception")

1. **Neutral Normal States:** When a KPI or shift is healthy/normal (`Định mức`, `Đã duyệt`, `100%`, `0 ca trống`), style its status pill with **neutral gray** (`background: var(--bg-input); color: var(--text-sub)`). Reserve `--c-coral` (Red) and `--c-amber` (Orange) strictly for **anomalies requiring action** (e.g., `Chờ duyệt > 0`, `Quên Check-out > 0`, `Thiếu người`).
2. **One Hero Value per Card:** Each Bento KPI card may contain at most **3 visual layers**:
   - **Header:** Icon + Title (`--text-sm`, weight `500`, `--text-sub`) + Status Pill on the right.
   - **Hero Metric:** Full-width single line (`--text-lg` or `--text-xl`, weight `700`, `--font-mono`, `tabular-nums`).
   - **Footer Submetrics:** Max 2–3 compact key-value pairs. **NEVER render fake random dot-matrices (`.dot-matrix`).**
3. **Action-First Ordering:** Always place actionable alerts (Pending OT, Hanging Shifts, Missing Roster Slots) ABOVE static analytical charts.

